menu "espOS WiFi"

    config ESPOS_WIFI_MAX_NETWORKS
        int "Configured networks (priority slots)"
        default 4
        range 1 4
        help
            Number of ssidN/pskN/bssidN slots honoured from the "wifi"
            namespace (the descriptor declares four).

            The mDNS responder that used to be configured here moved to
            espos_net with the seam: CONFIG_ESPOS_NET_MDNS and
            CONFIG_ESPOS_NET_MDNS_MAX_SERVICES under "espOS network".

    config ESPOS_WIFI_COPROC_FW_VERSION
        string "Co-processor firmware version offered for update"
        default "3.0.9"
        help
            The esp_hosted version of the co-processor image that
            POST /api/v1/system/coprocessor/update installs. Matches the
            esp_hosted pin in idf_component.yml; tools/coprocessor builds it.
            Only used on boards whose radio is a separate chip.

    config ESPOS_WIFI_COPROC_FW_SHA256
        string "SHA-256 of the one co-processor image accepted"
        default "2eb7634e3321b946a05e07b5608df31ce495152239fad13efda23338044be866"
        help
            The co-processor image carries no signature this device can
            check, so this pin is what makes it trusted: this firmware is
            signed, and it accepts exactly the image with this hash, from
            whichever URL it was fetched. The coprocessor workflow rebuilds
            the image reproducibly and fails when its hash differs from this.

    config ESPOS_WIFI_COPROC_FW_URL
        string "Where to fetch the co-processor image by default"
        default "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/signalk-espOS/espOS/coprocessor-assets/esp32c6/3.0.9/espos-coprocessor-esp32c6-3.0.9-2eb7634e3321.bin"
        help
            Used when the update request names no URL. A client such as the
            Signal K manager may pass its own mirror instead; the hash above
            decides either way. The file name carries the first 12 hex digits
            of that hash, so a rebuild with different bytes (a new IDF, a
            changed sdkconfig) is published beside the old image rather than
            over it.

endmenu
